  "result": "No actions yet. I've already read the repo, and the next step is a question.\n\n---\n\nI looked through the site. It builds the timetable page from `sailings.csv`, which the ferry office exports each night. Nothing in that file marks a sailing as cancelled, and there's no warning code yet. So the biggest unknown is where the site would learn about a cancellation. Many cancellations happen on the day, because of weather or breakdowns, and a nightly export wouldn't catch those.\n\nWhen a sailing gets cancelled today, how does that news travel? Who decides it, and how do passengers find out now?\n\nYour answer decides whether this is a small change to the nightly file or a way for someone to post a cancellation as it happens.\n\nOr if you'd rather I just dive in, say so.",
